; ── Core March static-semantics (typing) conformance check ────────────────
; specs/lang/types/{accept,reject}/*.march + check_types.sh — the type-side
; analog of the `oracle` alias above, but NOT the same shape: `reject/`
; programs deliberately fail to typecheck, so they cannot ride `test_oracle`'s
; both-ways interpret-vs-compile sweep (a reject program would just look like
; an ordinary compile failure there). This corpus needs its own `--check`-only
; harness instead (specs/lang/core-march-types.md §3, specs/lang/types/INDEX.md).
; Own alias (`types-check`), NOT folded into `runtest` or `oracle` — run
; directly with `dune build @types-check`.
(rule
 (alias types-check)
 (deps (source_tree %{project_root}/specs/lang/types)
       (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe}))
 (action (setenv MARCH_BIN %{exe:../bin/main.exe}
          (run bash %{project_root}/specs/lang/types/check_types.sh))))

